# Slint Kit

> {{ components.length }} native UI components for Rust and Slint: typed forms and validation, virtualized tables and lists, date and time pickers, exact decimal fields, dialogs, navigation and layout, with complete light and dark themes. Rust owns validated values and stable identity; Slint owns presentation and native interaction.

Current release: {{ project.version }}. Requires Rust {{ project.rust }}+ and Slint {{ project.slint }}. Desktop: macOS, Windows, Linux. Mobile: Android and iOS through Slint's mobile backends; device qualification is application-specific. Optional native file/directory dialogs return `SelectionOutcome::Failed(HostError::Unsupported)` on mobile. License: GPL-3.0-or-later; a commercial license is planned from 1.0.

Install with `slint-kit = "={{ project.version }}"` in `[dependencies]`, a compatible `slint` dependency, and `slint-kit-build = "={{ project.version }}"` in `[build-dependencies]`. Compile the UI with `slint_kit_build::compile("ui/app.slint")` in `build.rs`, import components with `import { KitButton } from "@kit";` and call `slint_kit::install(&window)` once per window before showing it.

